        "original_id": "18e367c0-c13e-56e3-8ad9-23565770c02a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lane Nishikawa\n- Products: Only the Brave\n- Organizations: 100th Infantry Battalion, 442nd Regimental Combat Team, 442nd Infantry Regiment\n- Events: World War II, rescue of the Lost Battalion\n- Places: Europe, Italy, southern France, Germany\n- Concepts: Nisei, Japanese Americans, segregated military units\n\nFacts:\n- Beginning in 1944, the 442nd Infantry Regiment fought primarily in Europe during World War II, especially in Italy, southern France, and Germany.\n- In 2005, Lane Nishikawa directed the independent feature film Only the Brave.\n- Only the Brave is a fictional account of the rescue of the Lost Battalion by the 100th Infantry Battalion/442nd Regimental Combat Team during World War II.\n- Only the Brave is a 2006 independent film about the 100th Infantry Battalion/442nd Regimental Combat Team, a segregated World War II unit primarily composed of Nisei Japanese Americans.\n- The 100th Infantry Battalion/442nd Regimental Combat Team became the most decorated unit in U.S. military history for its size and length of service.",
